ic displays in Valley Life Sciences Building, including a towering Tyrannosaurus rex cast in the atrium.","source_url":"https://www.lib.berkeley.edu/about/news/lgbtq-landmarks","source_title":"Places of pride: 10 LGBTQ+ landmarks to discover on the UC Berkeley campus","source_kind":"university_official","source_published_at":"2025-06-02","source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"The cited campus source describes the building’s public displays; visit during normal building access and observe posted rules.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"berkeley-rose-garden-stroll","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Berkeley Rose Garden Park","title":"Stroll the Berkeley Rose Garden","subtitle":"1201 Euclid Avenue, Berkeley","notes":"Take the terraced paths slowly, pause at the pergola or overlook, and bring water for the uphill walk through the garden.","short_summary":"A terraced city rose garden with Bay views, public paths, and a pergola.","evidence_claim":"The City of Berkeley states that entry to Berkeley Rose Garden Park is free.","source_url":"https://berkeleyca.gov/community-recreation/parks-recreation/parks/berkeley-rose-garden-park","source_title":"Berkeley Rose Garden Park | City of Berkeley","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"Entry is free. Listed hours are 6 AM–10 PM unless otherwise indicated; terraced paths can be steep.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"ohlone-park-green-space","subject_type":"place","entity_name":"Ohlone Park","title":"Spread out at Ohlone Park","subtitle":"1701 Hearst Avenue, Berkeley","notes":"Meet on the five-block greenway for a low-key outdoor catch-up, then use the open areas and paths while leaving shared spaces tidy.","short_summary":"A long city green space near campus with paths, gardens, play areas, and recreation space.","evidence_claim":"The City of Berkeley describes Ohlone Park as a five-block stretch of green space with recreational activities, play areas, a community garden, and an off-leash dog area.","source_url":"https://berkeleyca.gov/community-recreation/parks-recreation/parks","source_title":"Parks | City of Berkeley","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"maps_url":null,"access_notes":"A public city park; no admission is listed. Use open areas respectfully and follow posted park rules.","cost_status":"free","under21_safe":true}],"warnings":[]}],"warnings":[]}
